# Chroma library, modern Earth: NATIONAL ROUTE ENCOUNTERS, part a (v25 prep, draft 10-23; decision #11, cut item 3).
# For the Library, to pour into chroma-library/earth_national-a.lib (built as earth_national.py) once the protected
# text is in (briefs/NATIONAL.md). The routes' fields are Packs' (chroma-packs/national/, FIELDS_NATIONAL); only the
# moments are here. Routes 1 to 8 of world_fit.json national.routes: mandate_builder, public_service_architect,
# common_ground_maker, discoverer, systems_inventor, truthfinder, enterprise_builder, coalition_builder.
# Each route has four moments: its dilemma at the local step (rungs 0 1), the wider step (2 3), the national step (4),
# and one crisis (setback, rungs any). Each national moment reaches one of recognition, influence or authority.
# Layout: W U B R G once each, then one full cross cycle, alternating by moment:
#   s1: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W        s2: W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U        (16 moments each)

# ================================================================ MANDATE BUILDER (central promises versus coalition compromise)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mandate_builder: local, practice (s1)

== the open evening at the council rooms
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
route: mandate_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, public life
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, rival
earth: the weekly open evening on the council, where people come with the promise in their hands
tribal: the evening at the moot fire when anyone may come and ask what was promised
magic: the petitioners' hour at the town's council of the realm, when folk ask after a promise
scene: Every week {N} keeps an open evening at the council rooms, and every week the same question comes back: when will the late bus run again, as promised? The council's majority has offered weekday buses only, if {N} backs their housing plan at next month's vote.
scene tribal: Every few nights {N} sits at the moot fire for anyone who wants to ask, and every time they ask about the ford that was promised. The headman's kin offer half a ford, stones but no rail, if {N} backs their grazing plan at the next moot.
scene magic: Every week {N} sits the petitioners' hour at the town council of the realm, and every week they ask after the promised night ferry. The lord's men offer ferries on market days only, if {N} speaks for their new granary at the next sitting.
- W | answer every caller in person, and keep the full promise on the table | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | work out what the full route really costs, and bring the numbers | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | hold the housing vote back until the majority gives the whole route | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R | take the open evening out to the bus stop, and let people speak there | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson meet people where they wait | chance: 70
- G | keep the evenings to one a fortnight, and let neighbours bring the news | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 88
- W>U | write down every request, and report back on each one the next week | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson a list kept builds trust | chance: 82
- U>B | find the two councillors who could swing it, and learn what they need | v: self-direction, power | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- B>R | announce at the next evening that the deal is off unless the route is whole | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark made an enemy | chance: 55
- R>G | skip the meetings for a month, and ride the late buses that still run | v: hedonism, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- G>W | ask the oldest riders what they truly need, and promise only that | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 78
works: The evening ends with one more neighbour who believes the promise means something.
works: Nothing is settled yet, and {N} knows the route, the numbers and the people a little better.
fails: The same question comes back the next week, sharper, and {N} has no new answer.
fails: A long evening of complaints, and {N} goes home with the promise feeling heavier than before.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mandate_builder: wider, contest (s2)

== the district vote on the shared slate
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: contest
rungs: 2 3
fork:
route: mandate_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, public life
horizon: months
roles: colleague, rival, neighbour
earth: a district vote on a slate of several groups, whose leaflet waters the central promise down
tribal: the gathering of the valley's clans to choose who speaks for all, where the promise must be shared
magic: the choosing of the province's council, where several houses stand together on one roll
scene: The slate that took {N} beyond the town now stands for the whole district, and the vote is in six weeks. The other groups on it want the central promise, the late buses and the reopened baths, softened to "where funds allow" on the leaflet. {rival} is standing against the slate on that promise alone.
scene tribal: The clans of the valley gather in six weeks to choose who speaks for all of them, and {N} stands with three other families. They want the promise of the ford kept vague, and {rival} stands alone on it.
scene magic: The province's council is chosen at the turn of the season, and {N} stands on one roll with three lesser houses. They want the promise of the night ferry written as "when the treasury allows", and {rival} stands against them on that promise alone.
- W | stand on the slate, and say the full promise in every hall anyway | v: conformity, universalism | aim: try | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 55
- U | stand, and show each ward what the promise costs and what it saves | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 55
- B | stand, and make the leaflet's wording the price of joining the slate | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: person colleague | chance: 50
- R | stand, and run a loud street campaign alongside the slate's own | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: try | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 45
- G | sit this vote out, and keep the town seat and its people close | v: security, tradition | aim: skip | foot: lesson the town seat still counts | chance: 88
- W>B | accept the softer wording on paper, and fight for full funds once elected | v: conformity, power | aim: try | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 55
- U>R | stand, with one new way of paying for the buses kept back for the debate | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: try | foot: lesson a fresh idea wins a hall | chance: 50
- B>G | stand, and bring the town's old riders out to speak for the promise | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: try | foot: person neighbour | chance: 55
- R>W | leave the slate, and stand alone on the promise exactly as written | v: self-direction, conformity | aim: try | foot: mark made an enemy | chance: 45
- G>U | skip it, and spend the season learning how the district's money moves | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: skip | foot: door learned a skill | chance: 85
works not G G>U: The count is close, and {N} comes out of it with a district that knows the promise by heart.
works: Whatever the choice, {N} can look the town's riders in the eye about it.
fails not G G>U: The vote goes the other way, and {N} spends a quiet month working out where the slate lost the district.
fails: For a while {N} wonders whether the softer wording, or the harder one, would have been the wiser call.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mandate_builder: national, cost, fork pay (s1)

== the price of a seat in the coalition
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: cost
rungs: 4
fork: pay
route: mandate_builder
stages: adult mature elder
age: 28-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: community, public life
horizon: years
roles: colleague, partner, rival
earth: the coalition that runs the national assembly offers a place in its talks, if the promise goes to a review
tribal: the great moot of all the clans offers a place at the inner fire, if the valley's promise waits a year
magic: the council of the realm offers a chair at its long table, if the promise is set aside for a season of study
scene: The coalition that runs the national assembly wants {N} in its talks: a voice in the country's choices, from the next session. The price is written plainly: the central promise goes to "a review", and {N} answers for that at home. It would also mean weeks away each month, and {partner} has already asked how often.
scene tribal: The great moot of all the clans offers {N} a place at the inner fire, where the country's choices are talked through. The price is that the valley's promise waits a year, and {N} must walk home and say so. It would mean moons away from the valley.
scene magic: The council of the realm offers {N} a chair at its long table for the coming session. The price is that the promise of the ferries is set aside for a season of study, and {N} must tell the town why. The court is three days' ride away.
- W | join, and go home every month to answer for the review in person | v: conformity, universalism | aim: pay | cost: money .1, time .5, family .3 | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 70
- U | join, once the review has a fixed end date written into the terms | v: self-direction, security | aim: pay | cost: money .1, time .4, family .2 | foot: lesson a deadline keeps a review honest | chance: 65
- B | join, and trade the review for the coalition's next big favour | v: power, achievement | aim: pay | cost: money .2, time .5, family .3 | foot: person colleague | chance: 55
- R | refuse the terms in public, and keep the promise whole from outside | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: refuse | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 60
- G | let the national seat go, and keep the town and the people who voted | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson a mandate is kept close | chance: 88
- W>U | ask for a season to consult the voters, then decide on what they say | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
- U>B | refuse these terms, and draft a counter-offer that keeps half the promise firm | v: self-direction, power | aim: refuse | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B>R | join, and push the promise straight back into the talks from inside | v: power, stimulation | aim: pay | cost: money .1, time .6, family .4 | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- R>G | let the national road go, and hand the mandate to a younger local voice | v: self-direction, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson the promise outlives the promiser | chance: 85
- G>W | wait until the household can carry the weeks away, then ask again | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 82
works: The choice is made in the open, and the people who voted for the promise know exactly where it stands.
works: Within a season the decision has settled, and the promise still has a name attached to it.
fails: Some voters call it a betrayal and some call it stubbornness, and both letters arrive in the same week.
fails: The weeks away, or the weeks of waiting, wear on the household more than anyone expected.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mandate_builder: crisis, setback (s2)

== the promise the money ran out on
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
route: mandate_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: community, conflict
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, rival
earth: the money for the promised service is cut from above, and the people who voted for it fill the hall
tribal: a hard winter takes the stones meant for the promised ford, and the valley comes to the fire
magic: the realm's treasury calls back the coin for the ferries, and the petitioners crowd the town hall
scene: The district has cut the money that was meant for the late buses, and the promise {N} stood on is gone for this year at least. The hall is full for the public meeting on Thursday, and {rival} has printed the old leaflet on the back of the agenda.
scene tribal: A hard winter has taken the stones meant for the ford, and they have gone to the pens. The whole valley comes to the fire, and {rival} repeats the old promise word for word.
scene magic: The realm's treasury has called back the coin set aside for the night ferries. The town hall is crowded for the sitting, and {rival} reads the old proclamation aloud.
- W | stand up first, and say plainly that the promise is broken for now, and why | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 70
- U | show the hall exactly where the money went, line by line | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | name the people above who cut it, and make them answer for it | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark made an enemy | chance: 55
- R | run the first late bus as a volunteer service, starting this week | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | step down, and keep the friendships and the knowledge of the streets | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson a lost promise teaches care | chance: 85
- W>B | apologise in the hall, then go to the district and bargain for next year | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 60
- U>R | find a cheaper way to run fewer late buses, and try it within a month | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson a smaller promise kept counts | chance: 60
- B>G | spend the seat's own budget on a minibus for the oldest riders | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 65
- R>W | let the seat go at the next vote, and stay on as an ordinary member | v: self-direction, conformity | aim: stop | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- G>U | sit with the angriest callers one by one, and learn what was really lost | v: benevolence, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person neighbour | chance: 75
works: The hall is angry and then, slowly, less angry, and {N} leaves with the mandate bruised but standing.
works: A month on, the people who voted for the promise still stop {N} in the street, and some of them say thanks.
fails: The meeting goes badly, and the leaflet on the back of the agenda is what people remember.
fails: The trust that took years to build loses a little ground, and it will take a while to win back.

# ================================================================ PUBLIC SERVICE ARCHITECT (wider access versus delivery quality)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- public_service_architect: local, practice (s1)

== the waiting list on the clinic wall
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
route: public_service_architect
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, boss
earth: running a small clinic well, with a waiting list that grows each week from the next village
tribal: keeping the healing hut well, while families walk in from the next valley
magic: keeping the town's granary and its dole fair, while folk come in from the next village
scene: The clinic {N} runs opens at eight, and by nine the waiting list on the wall is full. Half the new names are from the next village, whose own clinic closed in spring. The nurses are good, and they are tired, and the quality inspection is in two months.
scene tribal: The healing hut opens at first light, and by midmorning the families from the next valley are waiting too. The two healers are good and tired, and the elders come at the new moon to see how it runs.
scene magic: The town's granary opens its doors at dawn, and by noon the queue reaches the bridge, swelled by folk from the next village whose own store burned. The clerks are honest and worn thin, and the realm's steward inspects at the season's turn.
- W | keep the clinic's own standards exactly, and take new names only as places open | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | time every step of a visit for a week, and find where the hours go | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | ask the district for two more nurses, and make the case loudly | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person boss | chance: 55
- R | open on saturday mornings for the next village, and see who comes | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 65
- G | close the list for a month, and let the nurses catch their breath | v: security, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 88
- W>U | set a fair order for the list, and post the rules on the door | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson fair rules calm a queue | chance: 80
- U>B | train one receptionist to sort the list, and free a nurse an hour a day | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- B>R | promise the next village a full service, and work out the how later | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- R>G | take a long walk through the next village, and listen before deciding | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- G>W | keep the regulars first, and help the village set up a weekly visit of its own | v: tradition, conformity | aim: ease | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 80
works: By the end of the month the list is still long, but it moves, and the nurses say so.
works: Nothing grand changes, and the clinic runs a little better than it did.
fails: The list keeps growing faster than the clinic can clear it, and the tiredness shows.
fails: A flat month: the same queue, the same complaints, and no time to think.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- public_service_architect: wider, cost, fork pay (s2)

== the budget that fell by a fifth
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: cost
rungs: 2 3
fork: pay
route: public_service_architect
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, partner
earth: the regional service's budget falls by a fifth, with every town still expecting its clinic
tribal: a lean year, and the healers of five valleys must be fed from four valleys' stores
magic: the realm's steward cuts the granaries' allowance by a fifth, and every village still expects its dole
scene: The clinic network {N} built now serves five towns, and next year's budget has fallen by a fifth. Keeping all five open means thinner staff everywhere; keeping the standard means closing two. The plan is due to the region at the end of the month, and every town has already written to ask.
scene tribal: The healers now walk between five valleys, and this lean year the stores can feed only four valleys' worth. The elders want an answer by the next moon.
scene magic: The granaries {N} set up now feed five villages, and the steward has cut their allowance by a fifth. Every village has sent a letter, and the plan is due to the steward by the season's end.
- W | keep all five open on the agreed minimum, and guard that minimum hard | v: conformity, universalism | aim: pay | cost: money .2, time .5, family .2 | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 65
- U | rebuild the rota from the figures, so each town keeps its busiest hours | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: pay | cost: money .1, time .5, family .2 | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | raise the missing fifth from local firms, in return for their names on the doors | v: power, achievement | aim: pay | cost: money .2, time .4, family .2 | foot: person patron | chance: 55
- R | refuse the cut in public, and keep everything running until someone stops it | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: refuse | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 50
- G | hand the network back to the region, and go back to running one clinic well | v: security, tradition | aim: stop | foot: lesson one service done well matters | chance: 88
- W>B | close two clinics, keep the standard, and bargain for a bus between towns | v: conformity, power | aim: pay | cost: money .1, time .4, family .2 | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 60
- U>R | refuse the trade-off, and test a travelling clinic for the two smallest towns | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: refuse | foot: lesson a new shape for service | chance: 55
- B>G | put in unpaid weekends to cover the gap, with the household's say-so | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: pay | cost: money .1, time .6, family .4 | foot: means time-.08 | chance: 60
- R>W | ask the region for one year's grace, and promise a plan that holds | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: ease | foot: door kept your word | chance: 75
- G>U | slow the network's growth for a year, and learn which towns need what | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
works: The plan goes in on time, and the towns grumble less than {N} feared.
works: A season on, the choice has settled, and the service is still there when people need it.
fails: Every town feels the cut somewhere, and the letters do not stop.
fails: The staff carry the strain for months, and two of them talk about leaving.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- public_service_architect: national, chance, fork take (s1)

== the country wants the model in every region
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: chance
rungs: 4
fork: take
route: public_service_architect
stages: adult mature elder
age: 28-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: work, public life
horizon: years
roles: colleague, boss, mentor
earth: the national ministry asks to roll the service out across the country within two years
tribal: the great moot asks for a healing hut in every valley of the land before two winters pass
magic: the council of the realm would have the granaries in every province within two harvests
scene: The ministry has seen the service work and wants it in every region within two years, with {N} advising on how the country's services are run. Two years is faster than good staff can be trained. They want an answer by the end of the month, before the next budget is set.
scene tribal: The great moot has heard of the healing huts and wants one in every valley before two winters pass, with {N} at the inner fire to say how. Two winters is too short to teach new healers well.
scene magic: The council of the realm wants the granaries in every province within two harvests, and {N} at the steward's table to advise. Two harvests is too short to find honest clerks enough.
- W | take it, with the service's standards written into every regional contract | v: conformity, security | aim: take | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 70
- U | ask for a pilot in three regions first, and decide on what it shows | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: lesson pilot before the promise | chance: 65
- B | take it, and insist on the right to choose every regional head | v: power, achievement | aim: take | foot: person colleague | chance: 55
- R | take it now, all regions at once, and train people on the move | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: take | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | turn it down, and keep the service where it is known and trusted | v: security, tradition | aim: decline | foot: lesson trust grows at its own pace | chance: 88
- W>U | accept, if the deadline moves to four years so staff are trained properly | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: door kept your word | chance: 72
- U>B | advise on the method, and let each region build its own version | v: self-direction, power | aim: take | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B>R | win the regions over one by one, starting with the hardest | v: power, stimulation | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- R>G | let the national road go, and teach the people who will run it | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: person colleague | chance: 85
- G>W | step back from it with thanks, and keep the home service steady | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: stop | foot: lesson knowing the limit is a skill | chance: 88
works not G R>G G>W: The first regions open slower than the ministry wanted and better than it feared.
works: Whatever was chosen, it was chosen for the people the service is for, and the ministry knows it.
fails not G R>G G>W: The new regions stretch everything thin, and the first reports are uneven.
fails: For weeks the choice sits uneasily, and {N} wonders what the country lost or gained by it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- public_service_architect: crisis, setback (s2)

== the man who waited too long
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
route: public_service_architect
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
