earth: an elderly man waits far too long for a visit the service promised, and the town asks how
tribal: an old herdsman waits far too long for the healer, and the valley asks why
magic: an old widower goes without his dole for a month through a clerk's slip, and the village asks how
scene: An elderly man in one of the smaller towns waited three weeks for a home visit that should have taken three days. He is recovering, slowly, but his daughter has written to the paper, and the review board meets on Monday. Everyone knows whose service it is.
scene tribal: An old herdsman waited half a moon for a healer who should have come in three days. He is mending, but his daughter has stood up at the fire, and the elders will hear it at the moot.
scene magic: An old widower went a month without his dole through a clerk's slip at the granary. He is well enough now, but his daughter has petitioned the steward, and the hearing is set for the week's end.
- W | meet the family first, apologise in person, and take the blame for the service | v: conformity, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 75
- U | trace every step of the three weeks, and find exactly where it broke | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | defend the service hard at the board, and keep the cuts in the story | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person boss | chance: 50
- R | do the home visits in person for a month, to see it from the road | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 65
- G | hand the service to someone fresh, and keep what it taught about care | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson every name on a list matters | chance: 85
- W>B | own the failure at the board, and ask for the money to stop it recurring | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 60
- U>R | build a simple alarm for any visit late by a week, and switch it on now | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson small checks catch big gaps | chance: 65
- B>G | take the daughter's side in public, and push the board for a fix | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 60
- R>W | step down from the network, and go back to work on the front desk | v: self-direction, conformity | aim: stop | foot: person colleague | chance: 85
- G>U | visit the man every week while he mends, and listen to what went wrong | v: benevolence, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person neighbour | chance: 75
works: The board hears an honest account, and the service comes out of it changed and still trusted.
works: The man mends, the gap is closed, and the next late visit is caught in days.
fails: The paper runs the story for a week, and {N} reads every line of it.
fails: The review drags on, and the staff work under a cloud for a while.

# ================================================================ COMMON-GROUND MAKER (workable settlement versus a stronger principle)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- common_ground_maker: local, contest (s1)

== the wall between two yards
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: contest
rungs: 0 1
fork:
route: common_ground_maker
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, conflict
horizon: week
roles: neighbour, friend, elder
earth: a long quarrel between two neighbours over a shared wall, brought to {N} to settle
tribal: two families quarrel over a shared pen, and bring it to {N} to settle before the moot
magic: two households quarrel over a boundary stone, and both ask {N} to sit between them
scene: Two neighbours on {Ns} street have not spoken in a year over the wall between their yards: one rebuilt it a foot onto the other's ground. Both have agreed to sit down with {N} on Saturday. Splitting the difference would end it; the plain truth is that one of them was wronged.
scene tribal: Two families have not shared a meal in a year over a pen built a stride onto the other's grazing. Both have agreed to sit with {N} before the moot. Halving it would end it; the plain truth is that one was wronged.
scene magic: Two households have not spoken in a year over a boundary stone moved a foot in the night. Both will sit with {N} at the inn on market day. Halving the ground would end it; the plain truth is that one house was wronged.
- W | sit them down, and hold to the old boundary as it was drawn | v: conformity, universalism | aim: try | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 55
- U | measure the ground first, and bring the old plans to the table | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | settle it fast, with each side giving up something it will not miss | v: achievement, power | aim: try | foot: lesson a quick deal holds sometimes | chance: 60
