- G | let this one pass, and keep the firm's own regions well served | v: security, tradition | aim: skip | foot: lesson not every prize fits | chance: 88
- W>U | bid jointly with two regional firms, each serving its own ground | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: try | foot: person colleague | chance: 55
- U>B | bid for the three regions the firm knows best, not the whole country | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: lesson the right size of win | chance: 60
- B>R | bid, and challenge the big firms' prices in public | v: power, stimulation | aim: try | foot: mark made an enemy | chance: 45
- R>G | bid with the stories of the firm's own people at the heart of it | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: try | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 50
- G>W | skip it, and back a smaller firm's bid with advice instead | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: skip | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
works not G G>W: The result is close, and the trade knows the firm's name now, whatever the agency decides.
works: The choice was the right one, and the firm goes on standing on firm ground.
fails not G G>W: The big firms win on price, and {N} spends a month explaining the cost to the firm's people.
fails: For a while {N} wonders whether the firm was too cautious or too bold.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- enterprise_builder: crisis, setback (s2)

== the year the orders stopped
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
route: enterprise_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: colleague, partner, elder
earth: a bad year: the biggest customer goes under, and the wages are due on Friday
tribal: a bad season: the river drops, the boats sit idle, and the families who carry the trade need feeding
magic: a lean year: the great buyer of the capital goes bankrupt, and the clerks' wages fall due
scene: The firm's biggest customer has gone under, owing three months of orders. The wages for forty people are due on Friday, and the bank wants to talk about the loan. The firm has stood through bad years before, but never one like this.
scene tribal: The river has dropped and the boats sit idle, and the twenty families who carry for {N} have stores for a moon. The elders ask what {N} will do.
scene magic: The greatest buyer in the capital has gone bankrupt, owing a season's goods. The clerks' and carters' wages fall due at the week's end, and the moneylenders are asking.
- W | pay every wage on friday, even from the owner's own savings | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 65
- U | go through every cost line, and find what can stop without losing a job | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | chase the debt hard, and sell the customer's unpaid stock to cover it | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark made an enemy | chance: 55
- R | launch a new line within the month, and sell a way out of it | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 45
- G | close the firm with every wage paid, and keep the people and the lessons | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson closing well is an achievement | chance: 85
- W>B | tell the staff the truth, and agree a shorter week with the bank | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 60
- U>R | find three new customers in a fortnight, through the firm's old contacts | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 55
- B>G | cut the owner's pay to nothing, and keep every job through the winter | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means money-.10 | chance: 65
- R>W | sell the firm to its staff, and stay on as an ordinary hand | v: self-direction, conformity | aim: stop | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
- G>U | ask the oldest staff how the firm survived the last bad year | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person elder | chance: 75
works: Friday comes and the wages are paid, one way or another, and the firm's people notice how.
works: A season on, the worst is past, and {N} knows the firm's bones better than ever.
fails: The bank is less patient than hoped, and the winter is a long one.
fails: Two good people leave for safer jobs, and the firm feels their absence.

# ================================================================ COALITION BUILDER (broader support versus organisational identity)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- coalition_builder: local, contest (s1)

== the vote for the housing trust's board
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: contest
rungs: 0 1
fork:
route: coalition_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, public life
horizon: week
roles: colleague, rival, elder
earth: a seat on the housing trust's board, won only with other groups' votes, which come at the price of the group's name
tribal: a place among the elders of the shared grazing, won only if the other families' heads agree
magic: a seat on the guild hall's board, won only with the other guilds' votes
scene: The housing trust's board has one seat open, and {N} stands for it on behalf of the tenants' group. The tenants alone cannot win it. Two other groups will vote for {N} if the group drops "tenants" from its name and becomes "residents". The vote is next Thursday.
scene tribal: One place among the elders of the shared grazing is open, and {N} stands for the herders' families. Two other families will back {N} if the herders stop calling themselves the first families of the valley. The elders meet at the next moon.
scene magic: One seat on the guild hall's board is open, and {N} stands for the carters. The masons and the tanners will vote for {N} if the carters drop their old banner and stand under the hall's. The vote is at the week's end.
- W | stand under the group's own name, and ask each group for its vote honestly | v: conformity, universalism | aim: try | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 50
- U | find out what each group needs from the board, and stand on that | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | agree to the new name, and take the seat | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: mark gave in to pressure | chance: 65
- R | stand on the old name loudly, and fill the hall with tenants on the night | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: try | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 45
- G | stay out of this vote, and keep the group close and whole | v: security, tradition | aim: skip | foot: lesson a whole group is strength | chance: 88
- W>U | put the name change to the whole group, and stand by what it decides | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: try | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 60
- U>B | offer a shared name with both words in it, and count the votes again | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: lesson two words can share a sign | chance: 60
- B>R | win the third group over instead, and leave the name alone | v: power, stimulation | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- R>G | throw a street meal for all three groups before the vote | v: hedonism, benevolence | aim: try | foot: person neighbour | chance: 55
- G>W | let an older member stand instead, and back them fully | v: tradition, conformity | aim: skip | foot: person elder | chance: 85
works not G G>W: The count is tight, and whatever the result, three groups have now heard each other out.
works: Whatever was chosen, the group still meets on Tuesdays, and still trusts {N}.
fails not G G>W: The vote is lost by two, and {N} spends the week working out which two.
fails: Some members think the choice gave too much away and some too little, and both say so.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- coalition_builder: wider, practice (s2)

== three groups and one aim
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: practice
rungs: 2 3
fork:
route: coalition_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, public life
horizon: months
roles: colleague, rival, elder
earth: the monthly work of keeping three groups bound to one aim across the region
tribal: the moon-by-moon work of keeping three clans pulling the same way
magic: the season-by-season work of keeping three guilds behind one cause
scene: Each month the tenants, the small traders and the carers' union meet in {Ns} back room to keep one aim: affordable rents across the region. This month the traders want the coalition to back their parking scheme, which the carers oppose. If neither gets what it came for, one of them will drift away.
scene tribal: Each moon the herders, the fishers and the potters meet at {Ns} fire to keep one aim: fair shares at the crossing. This moon the fishers want the others behind their new weirs, which the potters oppose.
scene magic: Each season the carters, the masons and the tanners meet in {Ns} hall to keep one cause: fair tolls on the roads. This season the masons want backing for a new quarry, which the tanners oppose.
- W | keep the meeting to the one shared aim, and set the parking scheme aside | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 75
- U | map what each group gains from the aim, and show it on one page | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | give the traders their scheme, and win the carers with something bigger | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | put the quarrel on the table, and let them argue it out tonight | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson open quarrels heal faster | chance: 55
- G | skip this month's meeting, and let tempers settle | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- W>B | hold to the aim in the room, and bargain with each group privately after | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- U>R | propose a trial: back the scheme in one street, and judge it together | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson a trial answers a quarrel | chance: 60
- B>G | ask the traders to fund the carers' minibus in return for their scheme | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 60
- R>W | open with the coalition's first win, and remind them why they joined | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: work | foot: person elder | chance: 70
- G>U | let one member from each group chair it in turn for a season | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: lesson others can carry it | chance: 80
works: The three groups leave still together, which some months is the whole achievement.
works: The aim holds, and one small thing gets done that none of them could do alone.
fails: One group leaves early, and {N} spends the week ringing round.
fails: A long, sour evening, and the aim feels further off than before.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- coalition_builder: national, round, fork round (s1)

== the old alliances that keep the door shut
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: round
rungs: 4
fork: round
route: coalition_builder
stages: adult mature elder
age: 28-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, public life
horizon: years
roles: colleague, rival, friend
earth: the old alliances of the national industry body shut the coalition out; but there is {aim.round}
tribal: the oldest clans of the great moot will not seat the coalition; but there is {aim.round}
magic: the old houses of the realm will not seat a kingmaker of new houses; but there is {aim.round}
scene: The coalition now reaches across the country and could move national votes, but the old alliances that run the national industry body will not seat it. The way round is {aim.round}, which would bring far broader support, and would also want the coalition's own name and founding aim off the letterhead. The national session opens in two months.
scene tribal: The coalition's clans now stretch across the land, and the oldest clans of the great moot will not give them a place at the fire. There is {aim.round}, which would bring many more, and would ask the coalition to set its own name aside.
scene magic: The coalition's houses now span the realm, and the old houses will not seat them at council. There is {aim.round}, which would bring many more, and would have the coalition lower its own banner.
- W | go through {aim.round}, with the founding aim written into the terms | v: conformity, security | aim: round | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 65
- U | study {aim.round} first: who runs it, and what it has delivered before | v: self-direction, security | aim: round | foot: lesson know an ally first | chance: 70
- B | use {aim.round} to force the old alliances to bargain | v: power, achievement | aim: round | foot: mark made an enemy | chance: 50
- R | take the coalition to {aim.round} now, banner and all, and see who follows | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: round | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | wait a year, and keep the coalition's own groups well served | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: lesson strength begins at home | chance: 85
- W>U | ask the old body for its reasons in writing, and answer each by next session | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: door learned a skill | chance: 75
- U>B | try {aim.round}, keeping the name for the founding groups inside it | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: round | foot: person colleague | chance: 60
- B>R | try {aim.round}, and enjoy beating the people who shut the door | v: power, stimulation | aim: round | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R>G | let the national road go, and give the coalition back to its groups | v: self-direction, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson the groups are the point | chance: 85
- G>W | step aside, and keep the friends the coalition made along the way | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 88
works not G W>U R>G G>W: The new way in is broader and noisier than the old one, and the coalition's voice is heard in the national vote.
works: Whatever was chosen, the founding groups know their name was weighed and not sold cheap.
fails not G W>U R>G G>W: The new allies want more than they said, and the first season is a tug of war.
fails: The shut door still rankles, and {N} keeps glancing back at it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- coalition_builder: crisis, setback (s2)

== the group that walked out
tier: life event
shape: any
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
route: coalition_builder
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: community, conflict
horizon: months
roles: colleague, rival, elder
earth: one of the coalition's founding groups walks out, saying it was never delivered for
tribal: one of the clans leaves the coalition's fire, saying it was given nothing
magic: one of the coalition's guilds breaks away, saying it was never served
scene: The carers' union, one of the coalition's three founders, has walked out: the coalition won rents for the tenants and parking for the traders, they say, and nothing for carers. They have told the local paper. Two smaller groups are asking whether they should follow, and the next vote is in a month.
scene tribal: The potters have left the coalition's fire, saying the herders and fishers took everything and gave them nothing. Two smaller families are asking whether to follow before the next moot.
scene magic: The tanners have broken from the coalition, saying the carters and masons were served and they were not. Two lesser guilds wonder aloud whether to follow before the next council.
- W | go to the carers first, admit the coalition failed them, and set a date | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 65
- U | list what each group has gained since the founding, honestly, and publish it | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | offer the carers the next big win, in writing, to bring them back | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 55
- R | call an open meeting of every member, and have it out in public | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson daylight clears the air | chance: 50
- G | let the coalition wind down, and keep the friendships it made | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson alliances end and friendships last | chance: 85
- W>B | hold the remaining groups to their pledge, and bargain with the carers after | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- U>R | find one quick win for the carers, and deliver it within the month | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 55
- B>G | give the carers the chair for a year, and put their cause first | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 60
- R>W | step down as broker, and let the groups choose a new one | v: self-direction, conformity | aim: stop | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
- G>U | sit with the carers' oldest members, and learn what was missed | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person elder | chance: 70
works: The carers come back, warily, with a promise and a date, and the others stay.
works: The coalition is smaller for a while and more honest, and it still moves on cue.
fails: The paper's story spreads, and one of the smaller groups follows the carers out.
fails: A month of phone calls and sore feelings, and the next vote looks harder.
